    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 261826\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1126 AM PDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Dangerous heat expected across the Mojave Desert through Friday. \n\n* Chances of showers and thunderstorms across the region today and \n  Wednesday, with gusty winds being the greatest threat.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package... \nLight easterly winds turn southeasterly around 8kts in the mid \nafternoon. These winds turn southwesterly in the evening. \nTemperatures look to peak at 00z, and cool below 100 shortly after \n04z. Expect winds to become light and variable for mid Thursday \nmorning become turning southerly and becoming gusty in the mid-\nafternoon.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Moderate to gusty winds \nbuild this afternoon with gusts peaking around 20 kts. KDAG which \nwont see gusts until the early evening. While most sites will see \nwind reduce into the night, KDAG wont see gust cut off until the \nlate night. Winds don't look to increase again until the late \nmorning and early afternoon on Thursday. \n\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Light\nand variable winds will continue through late morning when winds \nwill settle from the east. Winds will gradually veer throughout \nthe morning hours, becoming more southeasterly later this \nafternoon. Winds will swing to the southwest after sunset in a \ntypical diurnal fashion. Generally dry conditions are expected \nthough some cumulus build ups are again expected across the higher\nterrain. Temperatures will exceed 100F through 17Z-04Z. VFR skies\nprevailing with increasing high clouds tonight into Thursday \nmorning. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Typical wind patterns\nare expected today with winds generally under 10KT. Southerly \nbreezes are expected in the Colorado River Valley and Owens Valley\nthis afternoon with 15 to 20 knot wind gusts expected through \nsunset. KDAG will briefly gust out of the west to around 20KT this\nevening like they usually do, but gusts should end by 09Z \ntonight. Isolated convection will be possible in the higher \nterrain of the southern Great Basin and northwestern Arizona this \nafternoon. Erratic gusty outflow winds will be the primary \nconcerns with any storms that develop. Outside of areas where \nconvection develops, VFR skies will prevail through the period \nwith increasing high clouds tonight.\n\n&&\n\n.CLIMATE...Numerous climate locations have a forecast high\ntemperature and/or forecast warm low temperature within 3 degrees of \nthe daily record.\n\nThe table below shows the daily record maximum temperature and the \nyear the record was last set. An asterisk (*) denotes which records \nare in jeopardy (within 3 degrees of the forecast).\n\nMAX           WED, AUG 26 THU, AUG 27 FRI, AUG 28\n              Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)\n\nLas Vegas     109(2001)*  110(2017)*  110(2019)*\nBishop        103(2019)*  103(2019)*  103(2017)\nNeedles       122(1924)   120(1891)   116(2023)*\nDaggett       111(2011)   111(2017)   111(2017)\nKingman       106(2020)*  107(2017)*  107(2009)\nDesert Rock   106(2001)*  107(2017)   107(2017)\nDeath Valley  122(2017)*  124(1924)   120(2011)*\n\nThe table below shows the daily record warm minimum temperature and \nthe year the record was last set. An asterisk (*) denotes which \nrecords are in jeopardy (within 3 degrees of the forecast).\n\nWARM MIN      WED, AUG 26 THU, AUG 27 FRI, AUG 28\n              Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)  Record(Yr)\n\nLas Vegas     88(2020)*   87(2011)*   86(2019)* \nBishop        66(1988)    67(1970)    62(1970) \nNeedles       93(2011)    93(2011)    94(2017) \nDaggett       82(1981)*   81(2011)*   82(2017)* \nKingman       79(1945)    79(2020)*   75(2019)* \nDesert Rock   78(1985)*   78(1995)*   77(2011)* \nDeath Valley  98(1991)*   95(2011)*  100(2019)* \n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Gorelow\nAVIATION...Murdock\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
